    "result": "Done! I found and fixed the bug. Here's what happened:\n\n**The Problem:** When parsing \"39.95\" as a price, JavaScript's floating-point arithmetic resulted in `39.95 * 100 = 3995.0000000000005` instead of exactly `3995`. The validation check failed because that's not an integer. Prices like 12.99 and 10.99 happened to have exact binary representations, so they worked fine\u2014a classic floating-point precision issue.\n\n**The Fix:** I added `Math.round()` to three currency-to-cents conversion functions:\n- `parseEuros()` in src/money.js\n- `decimalCommaToCents()` in src/locale.js  \n- `cellCents()` in src/money.js\n\nThis ensures floating-point imprecision is corrected to the nearest whole number. All 50 tests pass and your original command now works: `subtrack add Gym 39.95 --since 2026-10-03` \u2705",
